## 🔬 Module-by-Module Technical Specifications

### 5.1 Spatial Router (`src/router.py`)
* **Purpose:** Resolves GPS `(lat, lon)` to an official Upazila or routes to the Global pipeline.
* **Tier-0 National Envelope Geofence:**
  $$\text{Latitude} \in [20.50, 26.70], \quad \text{Longitude} \in [88.00, 92.70]$$
  Any coordinate falling outside this box immediately exits to `GLOBAL_FAO_ECOCROP` ($< 0.001\text{ ms}$).
* **Tier-1 Broad-Phase Filter:**
  Scans pre-computed Axis-Aligned Bounding Boxes (AABBs) from `data/upazila_boundaries.csv`. Reduces 505 Upazilas down to 1–3 candidate geometries.
* **Tier-2 Narrow-Phase Ray-Casting (Jordan Curve Theorem):**
  Pure-Python implementation casting a horizontal ray from `(lat, lon)` to $+\infty$. For each edge $(p_1, p_2)$ of the polygon:
  $$\text{intersects} \iff (p_1.y > \text{lat} \ne p_2.y > \text{lat}) \land \left(\text{lon} < \frac{(p_2.x - p_1.x)(\text{lat} - p_1.y)}{p_2.y - p_1.y} + p_1.x\right)$$
  An odd number of crossings indicates the point is **inside**; even indicates **outside**. Interior rings (holes) invert the condition.
* **Performance:** Average resolution time: **$0.128\text{ ms}$**.

