### 5.3 Global Environmental Fetcher (`src/global_env_fetcher.py`)
* **Purpose:** Collects keyless climatology and soil data for any international GPS coordinate.
* **NASA POWER API Client:**
  - Endpoint: `https://power.larc.nasa.gov/api/temporal/climatology/point?parameters=T2M,T2M_MIN,T2M_MAX,PRECTOTCORR&community=AG&latitude={lat}&longitude={lon}&format=JSON`
  - Retrieves 30-year climate normals.
  - Corrects precipitation: NASA returns `PRECTOTCORR` in $\text{mm/day}$; converts to monthly totals:
    $$\text{Rain}_{\text{month}} = \text{PRECTOTCORR}_{\text{month}} \times \text{DaysInMonth}$$
* **ISRIC SoilGrids 2.0 REST Client:**
  - Queries `https://rest.isric.org/soilgrids/v2.0/properties/query` (with failover to `https://soilgrids.pixelgust.com/`).
  - Retrieves pH ($\times 10$), Sand, Silt, Clay percentages, and Cation Exchange Capacity (CEC).
  - Implements complete **USDA Soil Texture Triangle Classification** logic.
* **FAO GAEZ v4 Daily Tipping-Bucket Water Balance:**
  - Soil reference water storage capacity: $S_{\max} = 100\text{ mm}$.
  - Daily Hargreaves Potential Evapotranspiration ($PET_d$) computed from extraterrestrial solar radiation $R_a$ and temperature range $(T_{\max} - T_{\min})^{0.5}$.
  - Daily Soil Moisture Tracking:
    $$W_t = \max\Big(0.0, \; \min\big(100.0, \; W_{t-1} + P_d - PET_d\big)\Big)$$
  - Length of Growing Period (LGP): Day is active when:
    $$(P_d + W_{t-1} \ge 0.5 \times PET_d) \land (T_{\text{mean}} \ge 5.0^\circ\text{C})$$
* **Dynamic Cropping Intensity $K$ Mapping:**
  - $\text{LGP} \ge 270\text{ days} \implies K = 3$ (Triple cropping)
  - $165 \le \text{LGP} < 270\text{ days} \implies K = 2$ (Double cropping)
  - $60 \le \text{LGP} < 165\text{ days} \implies K = 1$ (Single season)
  - $\text{LGP} < 60\text{ days} \implies K = 0$ (Hyper-arid desert, fallow)

