## 🔄 Stage 4: 2-Year (6-Season) Combinatorial Agronomic Filtering

### Combinatorial Space:
A full rotation spans **2 calendar years** across **6 consecutive seasons**:
$$\mathbf{S} = \big( \underbrace{c_1}_{\text{Rabi}_1},\, \underbrace{c_2}_{\text{Kh-1}_1},\, \underbrace{c_3}_{\text{Kh-2}_1},\, \underbrace{c_4}_{\text{Rabi}_2},\, \underbrace{c_5}_{\text{Kh-1}_2},\, \underbrace{c_6}_{\text{Kh-2}_2} \big)$$
With Stage 3 pools ($|\text{Rabi}|=7, |\text{Kharif-1}|=5, |\text{Kharif-2}|=3$):
$$\text{Total Sequences} = (7 \times 5 \times 3)^2 = 105 \times 105 = \mathbf{11{,}025 \text{ permutations}}$$

### The 5 Hard Agronomic Filtering Rules:
The engine applies 5 consecutive filters, eliminating 99.6% of infeasible permutations and producing **30 to 50 biologically viable sequences**:

1. **Rule 1: Botanical Family Break Across Consecutive Years for Same Season:**
   $$c_1.\text{family} \ne c_4.\text{family} \quad \land \quad c_2.\text{family} \ne c_5.\text{family}$$
   *(If $c_3$ is non-rice, $c_3.\text{family} \ne c_6.\text{family}$).* Prevents soil-borne pathogen buildup (*Ralstonia solanacearum*, *Phytophthora infestans*, root-knot nematodes).
2. **Rule 2: Mandatory Nitrogen-Fixing Legume Insertion:**
   $$\sum_{t=1}^6 \mathbb{I}(c_t \in \text{Fabaceae}) \ge 1$$
   Ensures symbiotic *Rhizobium* biological nitrogen fixation, contributing $35\text{–}50\text{ kg N/ha}$ and preventing soil acidification from urea overuse.
3. **Rule 3: Root Architecture Alternation (Soil Profile Optimization):**
   $$\exists \, c_t \in S \text{ such that } c_t.\text{root\_type} == \text{"deep\_tap"}$$
   Deep taproots (Jute, Mustard) pierce the impermeable $20\text{ cm}$ plow-pan (*hard pan*) created by wetland rice puddling, restoring subsoil infiltration.
4. **Rule 4: Summer Pest Bridge Break (Kharif-1 to Kharif-2 Continuity):**
   $$c_2.\text{family} \ne c_3.\text{family} \quad \land \quad c_5.\text{family} \ne c_6.\text{family}$$
   Prevents unbroken "green bridges" across hot humid summer months ($35^\circ\text{C}$, $\text{RH}>85\%$) that cause viral vector explosions (Whiteflies, BPH, Stem borers).
5. **Rule 5: 365-Day Annual Calendar & Turnaround Feasibility:**
   For each Year $Y \in \{1, 2\}$:
   $$\text{Days}_Y = \sum_{t \in Y} \big(c_t.\text{duration\_days} + 10\text{ days turnaround}\big) \le 345\text{ days}$$
   Ensures a 10-day inter-crop turnaround for tillage/nursery preparation and leaves a 20-day buffer against monsoon delays, preventing terminal heat stress.

