## 📊 Stage 5: Multi-Objective Optimization & Portfolio Selection

### Objective Function $Z(S)$:
For each surviving sequence $S \in \mathcal{S}_{\text{viable}}$, computes the composite scalarized score:
$$\max_{S \in \mathcal{S}_{\text{viable}}} \mathbf{Z}(S) = w_1 \cdot \text{NormGrossMargin}(S) + w_2 \cdot \text{SoilHealthScore}(S) - w_3 \cdot \text{WaterStressPenalty}(S)$$

### Objective Component Formulations:
1. **Expected 2-Year Gross Margin ($\text{GrossMargin}(S)$):**
   $$\text{GrossMargin}(S) = \sum_{t=1}^6 \Big[ \big(\text{Yield}_t \times \text{FarmgatePrice}_t\big) - \text{ProductionCost}_t \Big]$$
   Normalized Min-Max onto $[0, 100]$:
   $$\text{NormGrossMargin}(S) = \left( \frac{\text{GrossMargin}(S) - \text{MinGM}}{\text{MaxGM} - \text{MinGM}} \right) \times 100.0$$
2. **Soil Health Score ($\text{SoilHealthScore}(S)$):**
   $$\text{SoilHealthScore}(S) = \min\big(100.0, \; B_{\text{legume}} + B_{\text{biomass}} + B_{\text{diversity}} + B_{\text{taproot}}\big)$$
   - $B_{\text{legume}} = \text{Count}(\text{Fabaceae}) \times 25.0$ (Max 50)
   - $B_{\text{biomass}} = \text{Count}(\text{Jute/Sesbania}) \times 20.0$ (Max 40, for green foliage drop)
   - $B_{\text{diversity}} = |\text{Unique Families}| \times 7.5$ (Max 30)
   - $B_{\text{taproot}} = \text{Count}(\text{deep\_tap}) \times 10.0$ (Max 20)
3. **Water Stress Penalty ($\text{WaterStressPenalty}(S)$):**
   - Boro Rice on High Land (`HL`): $+50.0\text{ pts}$ per season (severe aquifer depletion).
   - Boro Rice on Medium High Land (`MHL`): $+25.0\text{ pts}$ per season.
   - Boro Rice on Low Land (`LL`): $0.0\text{ pts}$ (surface wetland water).
   - Cash Vegetables in dry winter on `HL`: $+10.0\text{ pts}$.
   - Rainfed/low-water crops: $0.0\text{ pts}$.

### Final Portfolio Archetypes Delivered:
Instead of 3 minor variations, delivers **3 strategically differentiated plans**:
* **Plan 1: Optimal Balanced Compromise** (Highest composite score $Z(S)$)
* **Plan 2: Economic Profit Maximizer** (Highest 2-Year Gross Margin)
* **Plan 3: Soil Health & Low-Input Regenerator** (Highest Soil Health Score & Lowest Pumping Cost)

